# Handoff: ENG-2273, built on the ENG-2272 branch

**Next session's job:** implement [ENG-2273](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2273/scroll-to-and-highlight-the-matched-line-when-previewing-a-tagged). When a candidate result is selected in Advanced Node Search, scroll the preview pane to its tagged line and flash-highlight it. Read the ticket for Problem, Solution and Done When.

**Status of ENG-2272:** the foundation is done, committed, and **not pushed or opened as a PR yet**.

## Where the foundation lives

- **Branch:** `eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search`
- **Worktree:** `/Users/trang.doan/Desktop/code/discourse-graph/.claude/worktrees/eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search`
- **Commits:** HEAD is `4e06d408`, on top of `origin/main` `4a13294a`. See `git log origin/main..eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search`.
- **Reasoning layer** (approved plan, decisions, dead ends): `~/Documents/testVault/AI_sessions/AI engineering sessions/eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search/_context.md`
  - The user moved this folder. `~/.claude/scripts/session-context.sh resolve` still prints the old path `AI_sessions/eng-2272-…`, which is now an empty folder. Don't trust `CONTEXT_EXISTS=no` for ENG-2272.
- **Drafted PR body for ENG-2272:** `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-trang-doan-Desktop-code-discourse-graph/0126bbf9-c515-4274-91fd-18f8da370117/scratchpad/pr-body.md`. The scratchpad gets wiped between sessions. Copy it if it's still there; otherwise regenerate it with `/create-pr --dry-run` on the 2272 branch.

## Stacking the new branch

- Linear branch name: `eng-2273-scroll-to-and-highlight-the-matched-line-when-previewing-a`.
- Create it from the **local** 2272 branch, not `origin/main`. `/start`'s default is `origin/main`, so override it:
  `git worktree add -b eng-2273-scroll-to-and-highlight-the-matched-line-when-previewing-a .claude/worktrees/eng-2273-… eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search`
- The 2273 PR should target the 2272 branch once that's pushed. `/create-pr` infers a stacked base. Verify it; see memory `reference_create_pr_target_branch_drift`.
- If 2272 gets rewritten (rebase, review fixes), rebase 2273 onto it.

## What ENG-2273 can build on

- **Candidate data:** each candidate result carries `tagLine: { line, tag }`, the 0-based source line and the node-type tag.
  - Type: `DiscourseNodeCandidate` in `apps/obsidian/src/services/QueryEngine.ts`.
  - Produced by `QueryEngine.getCandidateNodes`: one pass over `metadataCache` tags, then `cachedRead` on the files that matched.
- **Preview:** `PreviewPane` in `apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSearchModal.tsx`.
  - It renders the **whole file** with `MarkdownRenderer.render` into `containerRef`.
  - Its effects re-run on `file` changes only.
  - Two candidates from the same file share a `file`, so switching between them won't re-trigger anything today. Scroll and highlight must also key on `result.tagLine?.line`.
- **Title rule:** `titleFromTaggedLine` in `apps/obsidian/src/utils/taggedLine.ts` produces the result title.
  - It strips list, heading and quote markers and every `#token`.
  - It does **not** strip wikilinks, bold/italic or inline code.
  - The ticket's text-matching approach needs rendered-equivalent text, so this title won't match rendered text for formatted lines.
  - It's shared with create-node-from-tag in `apps/obsidian/src/utils/tagNodeHandler.ts`. Don't change its output for that flow as a side effect. Add a separate matcher instead.
- **Opening at a line** already works: `openFileInNewTab/openFileInNewLeaf(app, file, { line })` in `apps/obsidian/src/components/canvas/utils/openFileUtils.ts`.

## Open design question to settle first

The ticket proposes finding the line by matching sanitized text against rendered blocks, because `MarkdownRenderer.render` has no mapping from source line to DOM node. We know the exact source `line`, so there may be options that avoid fuzzy text matching. Two examples:
- Render a sentinel near that line.
- Use the section and position info from `metadataCache.getFileCache(file).sections`/`listItems` to pick the Nth rendered block.

Neither has been evaluated. Confirm with the user before coding (they like ASCII sketches and short option lists).

## Reference and prior art

- John's draft PR for 2273: https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/pull/1449. It's stacked on his 2272 draft #1448.
  - We rebuilt 2272 fresh instead of using #1448, which had messy row layout, opaque sorting and a sanitizer that broke `snake_case` and URL fragments. Treat #1449 as reference only.
  - Its `scrollToAndFlashLine` idea and sanitizer are the parts to evaluate.
- Obsidian test vault slot 1 is `~/Documents/dgDevVault`.
  - It has seeded notes under `_verify/eng-2272-show-candidate-nodes-as-results-in-advanced-node-search/`. `zephyr-candidates.md` has a paragraph line, a list line and a `##` heading, each tagged, at lines 2, 3 and 4 when counting from 1. These are good fixtures for scroll targets.
  - Add formatted lines (a `[[link]]`, `**bold**`, `` `code` ``) to cover the ticket's sanitizer note.
- The ENG-2272 CDP scenario file was in the scratchpad and will likely be gone. Its helpers are worth recreating: open search, toggle candidates, `waitForRows`, `readRows`.
  - The driver's `evaluate` only adds `return` when the expression contains none, so wait predicates that use an inner IIFE must start with `return (() => …)()`.
  - The type-filter menu starts with all types checked. Clicking one *excludes* it.

## Environment gotchas from this session

- `.env` files are gitignored. `/start`'s copy loop silently copied none once. Check that `apps/obsidian/.env` has `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_VAULTS` and `OBSIDIAN_PLUGIN_PATH` (both point at dgDevVault).
- Only one Obsidian dev watcher may write to dgDevVault at a time. The main checkout (currently on `jsmorabito/eng-2272-tag-search-results`) and other worktrees also mirror there. Before trusting a run, grep the vault `main.js` for a symbol you just added.
- An ENG-2272 dev watcher may still be running from the 2272 worktree. Stop it before starting the 2273 one.

## Suggested skills

- `start`: set up the worktree. Override the base to the 2272 branch as shown above.
- `mattpocock-skills:grilling` or a short ASCII option list: settle the line-locating approach before coding.
- `mattpocock-skills:tdd`: agree the test seams first. The line locator is a good pure seam if it's extracted as a util.
- `dg-obsidian-cdp-verify`: live proof of scroll and highlight in dgDevVault. Measure `scrollTop` and the highlighted element's text.
- `checkpoint`: record the 2273 plan and decisions.
- `dg-pr-adherence-check`, `dg-delegated-full-review`, `scope-check`, then `create-pr`: before handoff. `create-pr` must target the 2272 branch.
- `obsidian-plugin-guidelines`: if the highlight adds CSS or DOM manipulation.
const LIST_INDICATOR_REGEX = /^(\s*)(\d+[.)]\s+|[-*+]\s+(?:\[[ xX]\]\s+)?)/;

const BLOCK_MARKER_REGEX = /^\s*(?:#{1,6}\s+|>\s*)/;

const sanitizeTitle = (title: string): string =>
  title
    .replace(LIST_INDICATOR_REGEX, "")
    .replace(/[\\/:]/g, "")
    .replace(/\s+/g, " ")
    .trim();

export const extractListPrefix = (line: string): string =>
  line.match(LIST_INDICATOR_REGEX)?.[0] ?? "";

export const titleFromTaggedLine = (lineText: string): string =>
  sanitizeTitle(
    lineText.replace(BLOCK_MARKER_REGEX, "").replace(/#[^\s]+/g, ""),
  );
